ar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-04-25T19:49:32Z","updated_at":"2025-04-25T21:15:24Z","body":"I have a theory!\n\n`dlsym()` is a no-op without `dlink_enabled=yes`, but with it, `dlsym()` will try to actually load a symbol.\n\n`OS_Web` descends from `OS_Unix` and I think it's `OS_Unix::_load_iconv()` running that's causing the error\n\nAll that stuff is wrapped in `#ifndef __GLIBC__`, but we probably want to wrap it in `#if !defined(__GLIBC__) && !defined(WEB_ENABLED)` instead.\n\nI haven't done any testing to confirm","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831308089/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2831310868","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/105766#issuecomment-2831310868","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105766","id":2831310868,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6owmAU","user":{"login":"marcosc90","id":8364242,"node_id":